  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=129",
      "html": "<p>Gymnallabes typus Günther, 1867. Size: 23 cm SL. Distinguished by the extremely elongate body, reduced cranial shield, confluent median fins, small eyes and presence of pelvic fins. Unpaired fins continuous, paired fins reduced or absent.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=129",
      "html": "<p>West Africa: lower course and delta of the Niger River and Cross River basin in Nigeria. Also known from Cameroon. Type locality: West Africa, probably Old Calabar. IUCN Red List category: Least Concern (last assessed 2019).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=129",
      "html": "<p>pH 5.8–7.0. Temperature 22–27°C. Sensitive to bad water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=129",
      "html": "<p>Provide plenty of driftwood for the fish to hide. Ensure that the tank cover is tight-fitting or weighed down, as they are capable of climbing out.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=129",
      "html": "<p>Will take all manner of pelleted food, as well as frozen and live food (the latter being preferred).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=129",
      "html": "<p>A peaceful fish that is best suited for the West African biotope tank. Ideal tankmates include mid-sized African barbs, tetras, and cichlids.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=129",
      "html": "<p>In ventral view especially, females are much broader in the body than males of equal age and rearing practices.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=129",
      "html": "<p>Not reported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
